# "Creatures your opponents control" - only creatures. Bot1's Nowhere to Run is cast on turn three and Bot2 responds with
# Dawn's Truce, so every permanent Bot2 controls has hexproof. Once Nowhere to Run has resolved, its enters trigger targets the
# Ornithopter (a creature, hexproof ignored) and, with the trigger still on the stack, Bot1's Disenchant cannot be aimed at
# Bot2's Mox Emerald: an artifact, not a creature, so its hexproof counts (the refusal, with the mana for it untapped).
# The trigger then resolves and the Ornithopter dies.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Nowhere to Run
Disenchant
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Ornithopter
Dawn's Truce
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nowhere to Run.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Dawn's Truce.Cast
Bot2.Decline
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Keywords = Hexproof
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying; Hexproof
Bot1.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Disenchant.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Dawn's Truce
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Keywords = Hexproof
